sted in sound and I've always been  interested in sound I've all but my  approach to music really started like on  the music theory side and then I play  several instruments but and I teach  music to my kids for example but I I'm  always really interested even in the  most basic ideas of music theory you  know Western music theory especially oh  yeah and Peter I found out has absolute  pitch as well which didn't hurt for this  role  I wouldn't test it right now but what  one at one of the daughter and my  daughter actually I think you know might  well say and so just I think about time  a lot but the when when Peter and I met  and first talked about the project it  was about a year before we actually  physically made the movie and I you know  once he was interested I just you know I  felt like it was my job just keep keep  that momentum going and he came over to  my apartment early on in the process and  we recorded the script just like this on  microphones just so I could start  hearing it and it was incredibly helpful  for me because suddenly you know we're  this is where you weren't acting or  anything it was just just good now  cold-read but I was barely even reading  it for the first time you know you work  on a script for so long and in this case  years I could just press a space bar and  start you know listening  to the movie and I had this kind of  radio radio play version of the movie  for a while and that kind of  transitioned into an animatic but was  really a good like a blueprint for what  we eventually did a year later I mean  for me you know I look for enthusiasm I  look for excitement I look for ideas  that I haven't thought about in terms of  them being films which this is one  characters that interest me I really was  fascinated with somebody that was so  dedicated to making other people feel  better you know like literally going  into their homes and adjusting their  toasters and refrigerators in the hope  that it would cure their anxiety to me  t